comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T23:21:37.857Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-10-24: canonical orientation, request-specific SDK/rollback search, fresh open and in_progress lists, and complete strict all-status read of 3083 items including 2799 closed and 14 canceled; no omissions or unreadable files. Exact GitHub issue and title checks found no existing owner for this delta. Closed SDK/bulk foundations were read live and remain completed. Source report retained in full; intake is not reproduction proof."
body: "Evidence: [checkpoint-artifacts.ts:30](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rl/blob/6de2805236f0d955cb49a476c4f5e8cdfd510a9a/checkpoint-artifacts.ts#L30), [src/blobs.ts:12](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rlm/blob/64d70bdc023db07be5973aaed19a96178b22554d/src/blobs.ts#L12), [engine/objects.ts:235](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/blob/a8afb1a283c1beac6cd8db1ffd1ef5a13c5196f8/engine/objects.ts#L235).\n\nProblem: at least three packages own digest addressing, immutable put/get verification, root manifests/reachability and artifact retention. The SDK provides atomic file writes, tracker locks and tracker workspace snapshots; it does not export a generic immutable blob repository with backend-neutral storage. A tracker snapshot is not an arbitrary payload blob. Draft API: a namespaced adapter with put(bytes), getVerified(digest), immutable references, bounded regular-file IO, caller-owned publication locks and explicit roots/GC dry-run receipts. Keep VCS framing, erasure denials/signatures and RL retention policy in their packages. Acceptance: equal bytes share identity, mismatched stored bytes fail closed, concurrent same-digest publication is idempotent, lost-lease publication is refused, GC never retires referenced blobs, and a non-filesystem adapter passes the same contract. No hosted backend support should be claimed until tested.\n\n\nSource: a read-only audit of 30 fleet extensions against the exported SDK of @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.10.23 (3,188 exported names); each of the three cited packages re-implements this primitive today."
